{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q010_rossmann_family_function_divergence","answer":"Verified SCOPe facts (release 2.08, stable label 2.08-stable; current periodic update 2.08-2026-08-16). All three named groups are families under the same superfamily and fold: class c (Alpha and beta proteins (a/b), sunid 51349) > fold c.2 NAD(P)-binding Rossmann-fold domains (sunid 51734) > superfamily c.2.1 NAD(P)-binding Rossmann-fold domains (sunid 51735). Within c.2.1: c.2.1.1 Alcohol dehydrogenase-like, C-terminal domain (sunid 51736; members include Alcohol dehydrogenase, Quinone oxidoreductase, Ketose reductase, FAS enoylreductase domains, plus automated matches); c.2.1.8 CoA-binding domain (sunid 51900; members include Succinyl-CoA synthetase alpha-chain N-terminal (CoA-binding) domain, Acetate-CoA ligase alpha chain AcdA N-terminal domain, several hypothetical proteins, automated matches); c.2.1.9 Potassium channel NAD-binding domain (sunid 63944; members Ktn bsu222, Ktn Mja218, MthK potassium channel-related protein, Rck domain of putative K+ channel Kch, automated matches; annotation 'automatically mapped to Pfam 02254', xref PF02254). Note that c.2.1.6 is NOT the CoA-binding family in 2.08; it is 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase-like, N-terminal domain (sunid 51868), so the three families must be cited by sccs c.2.1.1, c.2.1.8 and c.2.1.9. Homology endpoints for all three families and for c.2.1 report homology_implied_by_level true with no warnings and no heterogeneity flags; the fold c.2 annotation gives the core as 3 layers a/b/a, parallel 6-stranded sheet, order 321456, and notes that the nucleotide-binding modes of this and the next two folds/superfamilies are similar. The c.2.1.1 family carries the comment 'N-terminal all-beta domain defines family', i.e. family membership rests on the companion N-terminal (GroES-like) domain architecture, not only on the Rossmann domain itself.

Interpretation at the correct evolutionary strength. The deepest shared homology-bearing node is the superfamily c.2.1, so SCOPe asserts probable common ancestry among the alcohol-dehydrogenase-like C-terminal, CoA-binding and potassium-channel NAD-binding (RCK/KTN) domains. Because they are different families, SCOPe does not assert the closer, sequence-supported relationship: a biologist should read them as a divergent clade of a single ancestral dinucleotide-binding Rossmann domain, not as close relatives. The shared fold c.2 adds only the topological statement (same 321456 parallel sheet, a/b/a sandwich); because here the fold and superfamily coincide in name, the homology claim comes from the superfamily level, not the fold level. The picture SCOPe paints is one of functional divergence under a conserved scaffold: the same superfamily contains catalytic NAD(P)-dependent oxidoreductase domains, a domain that has been repurposed to bind coenzyme A in acyl-CoA synthetases/ligases, and a non-enzymatic regulatory domain of potassium channels that binds nucleotide ligands to gate the pore. The common ancestor is inferred to have been a nucleotide-binding Rossmann domain; the ligand specificity and catalytic role were not conserved.

Limits and unsafe transfers. (1) Function must not be transferred across families: superfamily co-membership does not imply that a CoA-binding domain binds NAD(P)H, that an RCK/KTN domain has dehydrogenase activity, or that an ADH-like Rossmann domain binds CoA. Ligand identity, catalysis, cofactor preference (NAD vs NADP), and the channel-gating role of the RCK/KTN domain must come from external evidence: ligand-bound crystal structures, biochemical binding/kinetic assays, mutagenesis of the glycine-rich dinucleotide-binding motif, and electrophysiology for the channel domains. (2) Structural templates are not interchangeable across these families: the core sheet is shared but loop regions, the ligand-contacting residues, oligomerisation (e.g. RCK gating-ring assembly), and the companion domains (the all-beta N-terminal domain that defines c.2.1.1; the transmembrane pore in channels) differ, so homology modelling or active-site transfer across families needs a verified alignment and conserved-residue analysis, not SCOPe placement alone. (3) The c.2.1.1 family comment shows that SCOPe's family boundary is defined partly by domain architecture, so a lone Rossmann domain without the N-terminal all-beta domain should not be assumed to belong to c.2.1.1. (4) Each family contains 'automated matches' proteins; these are valid SCOPe assignments but should be reported as automated if provenance matters. (5) Representative selection within each family must use retrieved ASTRAL SPACI/AEROSPACI quality records for every candidate; none were retrieved here, so no representative is ranked. (6) Fold annotation that other folds (next two folds/superfamilies) have similar nucleotide-binding modes is not an assertion of homology to those folds; relationships to domains outside c.2.1 remain a structural-similarity statement only. (7) SCOPe does not provide the phylogenetic or sequence-profile evidence underlying its superfamily grouping via the API; the curator rationale is not exposed, so a biologist wanting to quantify the divergence should use profile-profile/HMM comparison, structure superposition, and conserved-motif analysis as independent evidence.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=alcohol%20dehydrogenase-like&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA-binding%20domain&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=potassium%20channel%20NAD-binding&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA-binding&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1.1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1.6","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1.6/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1.9","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1.9/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.2.1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51734/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/children?limit=100"]}]}
